    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are preparing a briefing note for a sales development representative who is about to contact a new inbound lead.\n\nLEAD\nCompany: {{ $json.company_name }}\nIndustry: {{ $json.industry }}\nCompany size: {{ $json.size_band }}\nContact job title: {{ $json.job_title }}\nHow they run the platform today: {{ $json.deployment }}\nWorkflows in production: {{ $json.wf_band }}\nRegulated sector: {{ $json.regulated_sector }}\nScore: {{ $json.score }} — firmographic {{ $json.score_firmographic }}, governance {{ $json.score_governance }}, seniority {{ $json.score_seniority }}\nWebsite content: {{ $json.body_text }}\n\nCONTEXT\nThe product is a workflow automation platform. The free self-hosted edition has no usage limits, so companies do not buy for automation capability. They buy when scale creates a governance problem: audit logging, role-based access control, multi-team separation, secrets management, or a compliance requirement.\n\nTASK\nWrite a briefing note as plain text. No markdown, no bold, no bullet characters. Use exactly these five labelled lines:\n\nCompany: what they do, one sentence.\nWhy this scored high: name the specific signal that drove the score, referencing the sub-scores.\nLikely use case: one plausible hypothesis based on their sector and stated usage.\nOpening angle: one suggested first line for outreach, referencing something specific to them.\nVerify first: what could not be confirmed and the rep should check before reaching out.\n\nUnder 140 words total. Be concrete. If the website content is empty or unhelpful, say so explicitly under \"Verify first\" rather than inventing detail.",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": []
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
